# Next.js Authentication

**Trigger**: When modifying auth-related files, protected routes, or SessionProvider setup.

> **Aspirational**: This rule activates when authentication is added to the project (e.g., `src/lib/auth.ts`).

> **Server/Client Component Classification**: See [react-components.mdc](.cursor/rules/react-components.mdc) for third-party context provider rules. SessionProvider MUST live in a Client Component.

## auth() Helper Pattern

Use the `auth()` helper from the auth config in Server Components and Route Handlers:

```typescript
// Server Component
import { auth } from '@/lib/auth';

export default async function ProtectedPage() {
  const session = await auth();
  if (!session?.user) {
    return redirect('/login');
  }
  // ...
}
```

```typescript
// Route Handler
import { auth } from '@/lib/auth';

export async function GET() {
  const session = await auth();
  if (!session?.user) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Unauthorized' }, { status: 401 });
  }
  // ...
}
```

**Do not read session from cookies directly** — always use the `auth()` helper.

